/**
@page image_display_lifecycle From file selection to displayed image

This walkthrough follows the main window's static-image path. Animated playback
and source-tile views have additional update paths. Read @ref ownership_and_async
for the reference ownership, callback threading, and cancellation contracts.

@section image_lifecycle_steps Normal display path

<ol>
<li><b>Select a file.</b> layout_image_set_index() resolves an index in the
displayed list and chooses a read-ahead candidate based on navigation direction
and selection. layout_image_set_fd() calls image_change_fd() and synchronizes the
selection and sidebars. Updating ImageWindow's FileData reference does not mean
new pixels are displayed.</li>
<li><b>Reuse pixels or prepare a load.</b> In @ref image.cc,
@ref image_load_begin() first checks the decoded-image cache, then matching
read-ahead work. Otherwise it creates an ImageLoader, connects handlers, and calls
image_loader_start_deferred(), allowing rapid navigation to supersede the request.</li>
<li><b>Decode and report progress.</b> The loader selects an ImageLoaderBackend
and normally decodes on a worker. Main-context callbacks report dimensions through
@ref image_load_size_prepared_cb() and updated regions through
@ref image_load_area_ready_cb() and pixbuf_renderer_area_changed(). Progressive
updates can draw before decoding ends; delayed flipping retains the previous
image until incoming pixels are ready.</li>
<li><b>Finish decoding and prepare reuse.</b> The loader's done signal reaches
@ref image_load_done_cb(). When read-ahead caching is enabled, it retains decoded
pixels on the FileData and registers them with FileCache. It clears loading state,
installs the finished pixbuf when needed, releases the active loader, notifies
pixel consumers, and starts further read-ahead. It does not wait for screen
presentation.</li>
<li><b>Prepare the displayed composition.</b> image_change_pixbuf() establishes
orientation, stereo settings, color processing, and the renderer's pixbuf reference.
PixbufRenderer queues drawing; its backend scales visible regions, applies
post-processing, and creates immutable textures. Settings and image properties
select tile/two-pass rendering or an eligible source-texture path. See
@ref rendering and @ref renderer-tiles.cc.</li>
<li><b>Report render readiness and snapshot.</b> pr_render_complete_signal()
reports completion of the renderer's current work. @ref image_render_complete_cb()
forwards this through @ref image_complete_util(), which updates ImageWindow's
completion state and invokes its callback when applicable. GTK snapshots retain
render nodes/textures for presentation; render completion is not a compositor
presentation timestamp.</li>
</ol>

These stages overlap: a progressive render batch can finish before decoding ends.
The loader's done signal and render_complete are separate events, not interchangeable
indications that an entire image has appeared on screen.

@section image_lifecycle_shortcuts Cache and read-ahead paths

| Situation | Work that changes |
| --- | --- |
| Decoded-image cache hit | Skips image-file decoding. Display preparation and any required scaling, color processing, and texture creation still run. |
| Matching read-ahead loader is still running | @ref image_read_ahead_check() transfers that loader to the active image, reconnects handlers, and releases delayed area updates. It does not start a second decoder for the same request. |
| Read-ahead pixels are already complete | Uses the retained pixels immediately and releases the read-ahead FileData reference. |
| Thumbnail or similarity data exists on disk | This is distinct from the decoded-image cache. Thumbnail and `.sim` entries are not full-resolution decoded pixels for the main image. |

Read-ahead and decoded-image caching are bounded by the configured image-cache
budget. They reduce repeated decoding; they do not make rendering free. See
@ref caches for the separate cache APIs and @ref image_loading for loader APIs.

@section image_lifecycle_interruption Selection changes, errors, and closure

A new selection calls @ref image_reset(), releasing the previous active loader
and color-processing state. Releasing the loader's last reference cancels pending
starts and waits for decoding to stop. Retained presentation state can keep the
previous image visible meanwhile.

@ref image_load_error_cb() records the error and uses the common completion
cleanup path. A partial pixbuf may exist; if no decoded pixels are available,
a fallback image is installed. A displayed pixbuf therefore does not by itself
indicate successful decoding.

ImageWindow destruction resets the active load and cancels read-ahead and
transition work. Independent loader owners must still protect callback context;
see @ref ownership_loader and @ref ownership_renderer.

@section image_lifecycle_profiling Choosing timing boundaries

For performance investigations, record selection time, decoded-pixel availability,
and render readiness separately. A cached-image test should establish a decoded
cache hit before comparing rendering costs. Measuring actual visible presentation
requires GTK/GSK or compositor instrumentation in addition to Geeqie's completion
callbacks.
*/
